.wikipedia.org/wiki/JSTOR_(identifier)" title="JSTOR (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFbQ">JSTOR</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwFbU"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.jstor.org/stable/2009820" class="external text" id="mwFbY">2009820</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S2CID_(identifier)" title="S2CID (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFbc">S2CID</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwFbg"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusID:251572712" class="external text" id="mwFbk">251572712</a>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=World+Politics&amp;rft.atitle=Consociational+Democracy&amp;rft.volume=21&amp;rft.issue=2&amp;rft.pages=207-225&amp;rft.date=1969-01&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fapi.semanticscholar.org%2FCorpusID%3A251572712%23id-name%3DS2CID&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.jstor.org%2Fstable%2F2009820%23id-name%3DJSTOR&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.2307%2F2009820&amp;rft.aulast=Arend&amp;rft.aufirst=Lijphart&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cambridge.org%2Fcore%2Fjournals%2Fworld-politics%2Farticle%2Fabs%2Fconsociational-democracy%2FBB47BF2A5A4EBAE341FD3FA4E262410F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ADemocracy" class="Z3988" about="#mwt751" id="mwFbo"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Majoritarian_democracy_:0-235" id="cite_note-Majoritarian_democracy_:0-235" data-mw-footnote-number="232"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFbs"><a href="#cite_ref-Majoritarian_democracy_:0_235-0" id="mwFbw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFb0">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Majoritarian_democracy_:0_235-1" id="mwFb4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFb8">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Majoritarian_democracy_:0-235" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt757" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwFcA" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFDavid.2006" class="citation book cs1">David., Arter (2006). <i id="mwFcE">Democracy in Scandinavia: consensual, majoritarian or mixed?</i>. Manchester: Manchester University Press. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwFcI"> </span>15. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)" title="ISBN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFcM">ISBN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwFcQ"> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0-7190-7046-4" title="Special:BookSources/978-0-7190-7046-4" id="mwFcU"><bdi id="mwFcY">978-0-7190-7046-4</bdi></a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OCLC_(identifier)" title="OCLC (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFcc">OCLC</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwFcg"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://search.worldcat.org/oclc/64555175" class="external text" id="mwFck">64555175</a>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=Democracy+in+Scandinavia%3A+consensual%2C+majoritarian+or+mixed%3F&amp;rft.place=Manchester&amp;rft.pages=15&amp;rft.pub=Manchester+University+Press&amp;rft.date=2006&amp;rft_id=info%3Aoclcnum%2F64555175&amp;rft.isbn=978-0-7190-7046-4&amp;rft.aulast=David.&amp;rft.aufirst=Arter&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ADemocracy" class="Z3988" id="mwFco"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Majoritarian_democracy_:1-236" id="cite_note-Majoritarian_democracy_:1-236" data-mw-footnote-number="233"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFcs"><a href="#cite_ref-Majoritarian_democracy_:1_236-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwFcw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFc0">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Majoritarian_democracy_:1-236" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt764" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwFc4" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFReynal-Querol2002" class="citation journal cs1">Reynal-Querol, Marta (2002). "Political systems, stability and civil wars". <i id="mwFc8">Defence and Peace Economics</i>. <b id="mwFdA">13</b> (6): <span class="nowrap" id="mwFdE">465–</span>483. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doi_(identifier)" title="Doi (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFdI">doi</a>:<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://doi.org/10.1080%2F10242690214332" class="external text" id="mwFdM">10.1080/10242690214332</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S2CID_(identifier)" title="S2CID (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFdQ">S2CID</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwFdU"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusID:38417520" class="external text" id="mwFdY">38417520</a>. <q id="mwFdc">According to our model the proportional system has a lower probability of rebellion than the majoritarian system. ... Empirically, we find that countries with proportional system has the lowest probability that groups rebel and that the more inclusive is the system, the smaller the probability of suffering a civil war.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Defence+and+Peace+Economics&amp;rft.atitle=Political+systems%2C+stability+and+civil+wars&amp;rft.volume=13&amp;rft.issue=6&amp;rft.pages=465-483&amp;rft.date=2002&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1080%2F10242690214332&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fapi.semanticscholar.org%2FCorpusID%3A38417520%23id-name%3DS2CID&amp;rft.aulast=Reynal-Querol&amp;rft.aufirst=Marta&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ADemocracy" class="Z3988" id="mwFdg"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Majoritarian_democracy_:2-237" id="cite_note-Majoritarian_democracy_:2-237" data-mw-footnote-number="234"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFdk"><a href="#cite_ref-Majoritarian_democracy_:2_237-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwFdo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFds">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Majoritarian_democracy_:2-237" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt769" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwFdw" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFEmerson2016" class="citation book cs1">Emerson, Peter (2016). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://books.google.com/books?id=6txlCwAAQBAJ&amp;pg=PA48" class="external text" id="mwFd0"><i id="mwFd4">From Majority Rule to Inclusive Politics</i></a> (1st<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwFd8"> </span>ed.). Cham: Springer. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)" title="ISBN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFeA">ISBN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwFeE"> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-3-319-23500-4" title="Special:BookSources/978-3-319-23500-4" id="mwFeI"><bdi id="mwFeM">978-3-319-23500-4</bdi></a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OCLC_(identifier)" title="OCLC (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFeQ">OCLC</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwFeU"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://search.worldcat.org/oclc/948558369" class="external text" id="mwFeY">948558369</a>. <q id="mwFec">Unfortunately, one of the worst democratic structures is the most ubiquitous: majority rule based on majority voting. It must be emphasised, furthermore, that these two practices are often the catalysts of division and bitterness, if not indeed violence and war.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=From+Majority+Rule+to+Inclusive+Politics&amp;rft.place=Cham&amp;rft.edition=1st&amp;rft.pub=Springer&amp;rft.date=2016&amp;rft_id=info%3Aoclcnum%2F948558369&amp;rft.isbn=978-3-319-23500-4&amp;rft.aulast=Emerson&amp;rft.aufirst=Peter&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fbooks.google.com%2Fbooks%3Fid%3D6txlCwAAQBAJ%26pg%3DPA48&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ADemocracy" class="Z3988" id="mwFeg"></span></span></li>
