<li about="#cite_note-332" id="cite_note-332" data-mw-footnote-number="328"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwGls"><a href="#cite_ref-332" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwGlw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGl0">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-332" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1199" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwGl4" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFCassaniTomini2019" class="citation book cs1">Cassani, Andrea; Tomini, Luca (2019). "What Autocratization Is". <i id="mwGl8">Autocratization in post-Cold War Political Regimes</i>. Springer International Publishing. pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwGmA"> </span><span class="nowrap" id="mwGmE">15–</span>35. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)" title="ISBN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwGmI">ISBN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwGmM"> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-3-030-03125-1" title="Special:BookSources/978-3-030-03125-1" id="mwGmQ"><bdi id="mwGmU">978-3-030-03125-1</bdi></a>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=What+Autocratization+Is&amp;rft.btitle=Autocratization+in+post-Cold+War+Political+Regimes&amp;rft.pages=15-35&amp;rft.pub=Springer+International+Publishing&amp;rft.date=2019&amp;rft.isbn=978-3-030-03125-1&amp;rft.aulast=Cassani&amp;rft.aufirst=Andrea&amp;rft.au=Tomini%2C+Luca&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ADemocracy" class="Z3988" id="mwGmY"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Democratic_backsliding_Waldner-2018-333" id="cite_note-Democratic_backsliding_Waldner-2018-333" data-mw-footnote-number="329"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwGmc"><a href="#cite_ref-Democratic_backsliding_Waldner-2018_333-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwGmg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGmk">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Democratic_backsliding_Waldner-2018-333" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1204" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwGmo" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFWaldnerLust2018" class="citation journal cs1">Waldner, David; Lust, Ellen (2018). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://doi.org/10.1146%2Fannurev-polisci-050517-114628" class="external text" id="mwGms">"Unwelcome Change: Coming to Terms with Democratic Backsliding"</a>. <i id="mwGmw">Annual Review of Political Science</i>. <b id="mwGm0">21</b> (1): <span class="nowrap" id="mwGm4">93–</span>113. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doi_(identifier)" title="Doi (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwGm8">doi</a>:<span class="id-lock-free" title="Freely accessible" id="mwGnA"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://doi.org/10.1146%2Fannurev-polisci-050517-114628" class="external text" id="mwGnE">10.1146/annurev-polisci-050517-114628</a></span>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISSN_(identifier)" title="ISSN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwGnI">ISSN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwGnM"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://search.worldcat.org/issn/1094-2939" class="external text" id="mwGnQ">1094-2939</a>. <q id="mwGnU">Backsliding entails deterioration of qualities associated with democratic governance, within any regime. In democratic regimes, it is a decline in the quality of democracy; in autocracies, it is a decline in democratic qualities of governance.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Annual+Review+of+Political+Science&amp;rft.atitle=Unwelcome+Change%3A+Coming+to+Terms+with+Democratic+Backsliding&amp;rft.volume=21&amp;rft.issue=1&amp;rft.pages=93-113&amp;rft.date=2018&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1146%2Fannurev-polisci-050517-114628&amp;rft.issn=1094-2939&amp;rft.aulast=Waldner&amp;rft.aufirst=David&amp;rft.au=Lust%2C+Ellen&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdoi.org%2F10.1146%252Fannurev-polisci-050517-114628&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ADemocracy" class="Z3988" id="mwGnY"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-334" id="cite_note-334" data-mw-footnote-number="330"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwGnc"><a href="#cite_ref-334" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwGng"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGnk">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-334" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1209" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwGno" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFLindberg2018" class="citation journal cs1">Lindberg, Staffan I. (24 July 2018). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://carnegieeurope.eu/2018/07/24/nature-of-democratic-backsliding-in-europe-pub-76868" class="external text" id="mwGns">"The Nature of Democratic Backsliding in Europe"</a>. <i id="mwGnw">Carnegie Europe</i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20210413075045/https://carnegieeurope.eu/2018/07/24/nature-of-democratic-backsliding-in-europe-pub-76868" class="external text" id="mwGn0">Archived</a> from the original on 13 April 2021<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwGn4">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwGn8">27 January</span> 2021</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Carnegie+Europe&amp;rft.atitle=The+Nature+of+Democratic+Backsliding+in+Europe&amp;rft.date=2018-07-24&amp;rft.aulast=Lindberg&amp;rft.aufirst=Staffan+I.&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fcarnegieeurope.eu%2F2018%2F07%2F24%2Fnature-of-democratic-backsliding-in-europe-pub-76868&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ADemocracy" class="Z3988" id="mwGoA"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Democratic_backsliding_Rocha_Menocal_29–40-335" id="cite_note-Democratic_backsliding_Rocha_Menocal_29–40-335" data-mw-footnote-number="331"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwGoE"><a href="#cite_ref-Democratic_backsliding_Rocha_Menocal_29–40_335-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwGoI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGoM">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Democratic_backsliding_Rocha_Menocal_29–40-335" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1214" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwGoQ" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFRocha_MenocalFritzRakner2008" class="citation journal cs1">Rocha Menocal, Alina; Fritz, Verena; Rakner, Lise (June 2008). <span class="id-lock-subscription" title="Paid subscription required" id="mwGoU"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/10220460802217934" class="external text" id="mwGoY">"Hybrid regimes and the challenges of deepening and sustaining democracy in developing countries1"</a></span>. <i id="mwGoc">South African Journal of International Affairs</i>. <b id="mwGog">15</b> (1): <span class="nowrap" id="mwGok">29–</span>40. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doi_(identifier)" title="Doi (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwGoo">doi</a>:<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://doi.org/10.1080%2F10220460802217934" class="external text" id="mwGos">10.1080/10220460802217934</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISSN_(identifier)" title="ISSN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwGow">ISSN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwGo0"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://search.worldcat.org/issn/1022-0461" class="external text" id="mwGo4">1022-0461</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S2CID_(identifier)" title="S2CID (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwGo8">S2CID</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwGpA"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusID:55589140" class="external text" id="mwGpE">55589140</a>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20200121122048/https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/10220460802217934" class="external text" id="mwGpI">Archived</a> from the original on 21 January 2020.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=South+African+Journal+of+International+Affairs&amp;rft.atitle=Hybrid+regimes+and+the+challenges+of+deepening+and+sustaining+democracy+in+developing+countries1&amp;rft.volume=15&amp;rft.issue=1&amp;rft.pages=29-40&amp;rft.date=2008-06&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fapi.semanticscholar.org%2FCorpusID%3A55589140%23id-name%3DS2CID&amp;rft.issn=1022-0461&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1080%2F10220460802217934&amp;rft.aulast=Rocha+Menocal&amp;rft.aufirst=Alina&amp;rft.au=Fritz%2C+Verena&amp;rft.au=Rakner%2C+Lise&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tandfonline.com%2Fdoi%2Fabs%2F10.1080%2F10220460802217934&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ADemocracy" class="Z3988" id="mwGpM"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-336" id="cite_note-336" data-mw-footnote-number="332"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwGpQ"><a href="#cite_ref-336" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwGpU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGpY">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-336" class="mw-reference-text reference-text">
<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Remnick" title="David Remnick" id="mwGpc">David Remnick</a>: <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.newyorker.com/podcast/the-new-yorker-radio-hour/the-authors-of-how-democracies-die-on-the-new-democratic-minority" class="external text" id="mwGpg"><i id="mwGpk">The Authors of "How Democracies Die" on the New Democratic Minority - Two leading political scientists explain why voters failed to defend democracy: We never do.</i></a>, Podcast <i id="mwGpo"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_Yorker" title="The New Yorker" id="mwGps">The New Yorker</a> Radio Hour</i>, 15. November 2024.<br id="mwGpw"/>
Ursula Sommer discusses David Remnicks podcast with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steven_Levitsky" title="Steven Levitsky" id="mwGp0">Steven Levitsky</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daniel_Ziblatt" title="Daniel Ziblatt" id="mwGp4">Daniel Ziblatt</a> in: <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.wnycstudios.org/podcasts/tnyradiohour/articles/the-authors-of-how-democracies-die-on-the-new-democratic-minority" class="external text" id="mwGp8"><i id="mwGqA">The Authors of "How Democracies Die" on the New Democratic Minority</i></a>, 15 November 2024.</span></li>
